 and <strong>Roads</strong>?</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\"><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1902180/extras/8b62e7f6c5885c71999251760ec83798.poster.avif?t=1787393928\" width=600 height=270 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1902180/extras/8b62e7f6c5885c71999251760ec83798.webm?t=1787393928\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1902180/extras/8b62e7f6c5885c71999251760ec83798.mp4?t=1787393928\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Refine Metals for Tools &amp; Weapons</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >As your Plebs mine deeper into the ground they will discover a variety of <strong>different metals</strong>. Providing your workers and soldiers with <strong>higher quality metals</strong> makes them more effective, and you can even enhance your Plebs' <strong>metalworking skills</strong> to enable stronger tools &amp; weapons!</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Will you train a mighty force with the strongest metal weaponry, create a horde of weaker units to quickly overwhelm your enemies, or try to strike a balance between offence and defence? Each unit type has <strong>strengths and weaknesses</strong>, so careful army composition is vital to counter enemy forces effectively.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\"><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1902180/extras/c443772372786cf7a5e6ff4300f9cc5b.poster.avif?t=1787393928\" width=600 height=270 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1902180/extras/c443772372786cf7a5e6ff4300f9cc5b.webm?t=1787393928\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><sou